# What the API image must NOT carry.
#
# The starting point is that the build context is the whole repo and the image
# needs four things: requirements.txt, app/, run_api.py, and nothing else. The
# entries below are therefore about what would be harmful or wasteful if it
# slipped in, not an exhaustive mirror of .gitignore.

# --- Secrets ------------------------------------------------------------------
# .env holds the service-role key, which carries BYPASSRLS. It reaches the
# container as an environment variable set by the host, never as a baked layer:
# an image layer is readable by anyone who can pull the image, and deleting the
# file in a later layer does not remove it from the earlier one.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# --- Operator tooling that can act outside the system -------------------------
# tools/agentmail.py can send mail. CLAUDE.md R3 keeps send-capable code out of
# anything an agent can reach; leaving it out of the image keeps it out of
# anything the running service can reach. tools/load_data.py and the ingestion
# CLI likewise write to the database from a terminal, not from a request.
tools/

# --- Not the service ----------------------------------------------------------
frontend/
supabase/
tests/
docs/
reference/
.github/
.claude/

# --- Build and cache noise ----------------------------------------------------
.git/
.gitignore
.venv/
venv/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
htmlcov/
.coverage
*.egg-info/
dist/
build/
node_modules/
graphify-out/
audits/

# --- Editor / OS --------------------------------------------------------------
.idea/
.vscode/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
